<article class="env-lemma" id="0AMN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AMN">Lemma <span data-tag="0AMN">80.3.10</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $a : F \to G$ and $b : G \to H$ be transformations of functors $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}^{opp} \to \textit{Sets}$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\Delta : G \to G \times _ H G$ is representable by algebraic spaces, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$b \circ a : F \to H$ is representable by algebraic spaces. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $a$ is representable by algebraic spaces. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U$ be a scheme over $S$ and let $\xi \in G(U)$. Then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  U \times _{\xi , G, a} F = (U \times _{b(\xi ), H, b \circ a} F) \times _{(\xi , a), (G \times _ H G), \Delta } G  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Hence the result using Lemma <a href="/tag/03XY" data-tag="03XY">80.3.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>